# Property API requests (Chapter 7). Run with the REST Client extension
# in VS Code or the .http editor in Visual Studio.
@host = http://localhost:7071/api
@code = HBR-0042

### List available properties in Leeds, two or more bedrooms
GET {{host}}/v1/properties?city=Leeds&status=Available&minBedrooms=2&pageSize=20

### Read one property (note the ETag header)
GET {{host}}/v1/properties/{{code}}

### Create a property
POST {{host}}/v1/properties
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "code": "HBR-0099",
  "name": "7 Dock Street",
  "city": "Leeds",
  "postcode": "LS10 1JF",
  "bedrooms": 1,
  "monthlyRent": 875,
  "availableFrom": "2026-12-01"
}

### Change the rent, but only if nobody else has saved since our GET
PATCH {{host}}/v1/properties/{{code}}
Content-Type: application/json
If-Match: "<etag-from-the-get>"

{ "monthlyRent": 1195 }
